<%#
  PHOTOS (stage 4, S4-1): the gallery the public page has had since S3-4, on the maker's own page.
  Rows come from Maker::ProjectPhotos (ProjectsController#show → @photo_rows): the folder's image
  rows plus every live entry photo, deduped, name-ordered. Omitted entirely when there are none — a
  gallery with no pictures is not a quiet panel, it is no panel.

  Its own `thumbs` controller: this section sits OUTSIDE the Files panel's polling wrapper, the same
  reason projects/_log_entry carries one. Every row's thumbnail is already in @page_thumbs, because
  @photo_rows is its own term in ProjectsController#show's union (an image inside a browsed
  repository is drawn by no tile, so nothing else would put it there), so this polls the pending
  ones and never builds a second ThumbnailMap.
%>
<% if @photo_rows.any? %>
  <%# `project-photos` IS THE CONTENTS COLUMN'S ANCHOR (ProjectsHelper::SECTION_ANCHORS, 2026-11-19). %>
  <section class="panel photos-panel" id="project-photos">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <h2><%= panel_title(@panel_layout, "photos") %></h2>
      <%= section_note("photos", @photo_rows.size, pluralize(@photo_rows.size, "photo")) %>
    </div>
    <%= panel_intro(@panel_layout, "photos") %>
    <div class="project-photos" data-controller="thumbs" data-thumbs-url-value="<%= thumbnails_files_path %>">
      <% @photo_rows.each do |row| %>
        <%# NAMED BY THE FILE (the UX audit's §I): the picture inside carries an empty alt, so a
            `title` alone left a link a screen reader announced as nothing. %>
        <%= link_to file_path(row.node_id), class: "photo-cell file-cell", title: row.node.name, "aria-label": row.node.name,
                    data: file_open_data(thumb_cell_data(row.node_id, "IMG")) do %>
          <%= render "files/thumb", thumb: @page_thumbs.thumb(row.node_id), ext_label: "IMG",
                     url: preview_src(@page_thumbs.thumb(row.node_id)) %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>
<% end %>
